{{- /*
  profile-traits — the single source of truth mapping a profile to its
  traits. Usage (any file template, run-script, or .chezmoiignore):

      {{`{{- $traits := includeTemplate "profile-traits.tmpl" . | fromJson -}}`}}
      {{`{{- if $traits.headless }}…{{ end }}`}}

  Traits:
    headless   no interactive human desktop session. Gates GUI-app configs
               (WezTerm/Ghostty/espanso/Hammerspoon), tab-edit, .desktop
               registration, the TM scrub UX, and the human-machine pi
               home. A JetKVM console or a kiosk/status side-screen does
               NOT flip this — it is about a human driving a desktop
               session, not about attached displays.
    ephemeral  disposable work sandbox (dev-shell): prunable state, snap
               ecosystem, the 90-prune script.
    devTooling utilities and IDE-like packages used to develop ON the
               machine: hyperfine/git-cliff/ast-grep/grex/onefetch in the
               headless toolbox, tokei/tree-sitter-cli/kdl-lsp/usvg in the
               Cargofile, the LSP packages in the Npmfile, nvim's
               Mason/LSP/DAP/lint/format layer. Toolchains (go, rust, node,
               python, java, kotlin, lua, uv) are NOT dev tooling: they build
               the toolbox itself and stay everywhere.
    aiTooling  agent harnesses and everything that only serves them: pi and
               claude (Npmfile), ai-playbook (Gofile), ~/.pi, ~/.claude,
               ~/.config/{ai-playbook,agent-skills,pi-memctx}, AGENTS.md,
               the ai-commit dispatcher, the palette's agent entries, nvim's
               AI plugin, the CONTEXT7 secret.

  server = headless + dev + ai (the full-blown headless box);
  appliance = headless only (a box nobody develops on).

  Work tooling (Cursor, acli skills) is deliberately NOT a trait here:
  those gates stay as positive `eq .profile "work"` checks, which already
  fail closed.

  Unknown profiles FAIL the render: a typo'd or future profile must be
  added here deliberately, picking each trait. This is the fail-closed
  guarantee that replaced the old `ne .profile "dev-shell"`-style gates.

  The init template (.chezmoi.toml.tmpl) keeps a local two-line headless
  derivation instead of including this file — at init time the data this
  helper is fed from does not exist yet. Keep the two in sync.
*/ -}}
{{- $p := .profile -}}
{{- if eq $p "personal" "work" -}}
{"headless": false, "ephemeral": false, "devTooling": true, "aiTooling": true}
{{- else if eq $p "dev-shell" -}}
{"headless": true, "ephemeral": true, "devTooling": true, "aiTooling": true}
{{- else if eq $p "server" -}}
{"headless": true, "ephemeral": false, "devTooling": true, "aiTooling": true}
{{- else if eq $p "appliance" -}}
{"headless": true, "ephemeral": false, "devTooling": false, "aiTooling": false}
{{- else -}}
{{- fail (printf "profile-traits: unknown profile %q" $p) -}}
{{- end -}}
